{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Product page (PDP)

  Replaces the legacy chain (product-template.liquid -> product-extended.liquid,
  jQuery + Shopify.OptionSelectors) for templates/product.json's "main" slot.
  The old files are untouched and remain the rollback path: point main.type back
  at "product-template" and the legacy page returns.

  Load-bearing decisions — undo any of these and something distant breaks:

  1. ONE {% form 'product' %} holds the hidden [name="id"], the quantity input,
     the Add to Cart submit AND {{ form | payment_button }}. The legacy layout
     nested the payment form inside a hand-written cart form, so Buy It Now
     always bought the first variant regardless of selection. The pack radios
     are deliberately NOT named "id": Shopify's hosted wallet JS reads the
     form's [name=id], and a radio group would hand it the first radio rather
     than the checked one. assets/sh-product.js syncs the hidden input instead.

  2. The AJAX cart is inherited, not reimplemented. assets/ajax-cart.js.liquid
     delegates on body for `form[action^="/cart/add"]` submissions — serialize,
     POST /cart/add.js, open the drawer, update .enj-cartcount, dispatch
     'cart:updated'. This section only has to render a real form. The submit
     button carries .enj-add-to-cart-btn so ajax-cart applies its busy states,
     and [name="add"] means assets/hov-cart-checkout.js converts it into its
     .hov-cart__btn span structure (loading/success driven by 'cart:add').
     That conversion REWRITES the button's innerHTML — which is why the label
     is plain text with no icon, and why sh-product.js updates the label via
     .hov-cart__btn-default when present. shudhi-product.css repaints the
     converted button gold, the same scoped-repaint bargain
     .sh-signature .sh-btn--solid makes with the shared button component.

  3. The sticky bar's button is type="button" with a class that matches NEITHER
     ajax-cart's .enj-add-to-cart-btn NOR hov-cart-checkout's selector list.
     It fires a synthetic click() on the real submit button so the one real
     flow runs and the one real button shows the busy state (hov-cart-checkout
     enters "loading" from the click event, so requestSubmit() would skip it).
     Give it either class and the add fires twice / converts twice.

  4. Class naming is part of the wishlist contract. hov-wishlist.js scrapes
     btn.closest('[class*="card"], [class*="product"], li, article') and then
     reads an <img>, a '[class*="price"]:not([class*="compare"])' and an
     'a[href*="/products/"]' from whatever that resolves to. The root carries
     "product"; every inner wrapper uses the sh-pdp__ prefix precisely so
     closest() falls through to the root, where the gallery image, the main
     .sh-pdp__price and the breadcrumb's self-link live. The struck compare-at
     numbers are .sh-pdp__was — no "price" or "compare" substring — so the
     scrape can never pick a pack card's number over the real price.

  5. The countdown card ships with the `hidden` attribute and JS removes it
     only for a valid FUTURE deadline. This inverts the theme's fail-open rule
     on purpose: a timer frozen at a fake value (JS off, bad date) is worse
     than no timer. The deadline is one absolute moment from section settings —
     it survives refreshes and never re-seeds per pageload.

  6. The breadcrumb is its own markup (.sh-pdp__crumbs), never the shared
     snippets/breadcrumb.liquid classes: engo-customizes.css.liquid:35470+
     styles `.template-product .hov-breadcrumb` as a grey pill entirely in
     !important, and out-specifying that is a war not worth fighting.

  7. The star row, the short description and the FAQ under Buy it now are
     merchant content in templates/product.json (section settings + blocks),
     so they apply to EVERY product rendered by product.json. A second
     product needs its own product.<name>.json, or the custom.short_description
     metafield, which overrides the section's copy. The manual rating numbers
     are display-only: layout/theme.liquid emits aggregateRating solely from
     the reviews.rating / reviews.rating_count metafields a reviews app writes.

  8. Gallery order is product media first, then any gallery_image blocks
     (data-media-id="b-<block id>"), in the stage AND the thumb rail alike.
     The rail is rendered after the stage so the first <img> in the section
     stays the main 1100px image (note 4, and the LCP element). The Zoom
     viewer is a native <dialog>: every close path ends in dialog.close() and
     the one 'close' listener does the teardown; its scroll lock is a class on
     <html>, never body.style.overflow, which three theme scripts already write.

  Heading outline: h1 = product title (this is the page's h1 — the legacy
  layout used h1 here too), h2 = "Frequently asked questions" (visually
  hidden), the why panel and Reviews, h3 = FAQ questions and why items.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'shudhi-product.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}

{%- liquid
  # Initial variant: an explicit ?variant= URL wins, else the merchant's
  # "most popular" pick (if it exists and is buyable), else Shopify's default.
  assign initial = product.selected_variant
  if initial == blank
    assign mp_index = s.most_popular_position | minus: 1
    if product.variants.size > mp_index
      assign mp_variant = product.variants[mp_index]
      if mp_variant.available
        assign initial = mp_variant
      endif
    endif
  endif
  if initial == blank
    assign initial = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  endif

  # Rating: real app data (Shopify's standard reviews.* definitions, written
  # by Judge.me and friends) wins; the section's manual numbers fall back;
  # nothing renders at count 0.
  assign rv = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value
  assign rc = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | plus: 0
  assign rating_real = false
  if rv.rating != blank and rc > 0
    assign rating_val = rv.rating | times: 1.0
    assign rating_max = rv.scale_max | default: 5 | times: 1.0
    assign rating_count = rc
    assign rating_real = true
  else
    assign rating_val = s.rating_value | times: 1.0
    assign rating_max = 5.0
    assign rating_count = s.rating_count | plus: 0
  endif
  assign rating_pct = rating_val | divided_by: rating_max | times: 100 | round: 1
  assign rating_txt = rating_val | round: 1
  assign show_rating = false
  if rating_count > 0 and rating_val > 0
    assign show_rating = true
  endif

  # The Reviews block renders only when it has something to show, and the
  # review count links to it only then.
  assign show_reviews = false
  if s.show_reviews
    if rating_real or product.metafields.judgeme.widget != blank
      assign show_reviews = true
    endif
  endif

  # Block families rendered in different places — counted first (never
  # `where`), so an empty family leaves no empty box behind.
  assign gallery_extra = 0
  assign perk_count = 0
  assign why_count = 0
  assign avatar_count = 0
  for block in section.blocks
    case block.type
      when 'gallery_image'
        if block.settings.image != blank
          assign gallery_extra = gallery_extra | plus: 1
        endif
      when 'perk'
        if block.settings.title != blank
          assign perk_count = perk_count | plus: 1
        endif
      when 'why'
        if block.settings.title != blank
          assign why_count = why_count | plus: 1
        endif
      when 'avatar'
        assign avatar_count = avatar_count | plus: 1
    endcase
  endfor
  assign gallery_count = product.media.size | plus: gallery_extra

  # Checkout coupon, in cents, resolved once and read by the pack cards and the
  # strip under them. This is a REAL Shopify discount code the merchant creates
  # in admin — the theme only advertises it, it can never apply it. A blank code
  # or a zero amount switches every coupon line off in one place.
  assign coupon_cents = 0
  if s.coupon_enable and s.coupon_code != blank and s.coupon_value > 0
    assign coupon_cents = s.coupon_value | times: 100
  endif
-%}

<section class="sh sh-product sh-pdp"
         data-sh-pdp
         data-sh-money="{{ shop.money_format | escape }}"
         data-sh-money-currency="{{ shop.money_with_currency_format | escape }}"
         style="--sh-pdp-bg:{{ s.bg }};--sh-pdp-pad-top:{{ s.pad_top }}px;--sh-pdp-pad-bottom:{{ s.pad_bottom }}px;">
  <div class="sh-wrap">

    {%- comment -%} One star glyph + gold gradient shared by the rating row and
        the proof bar; a zero-size svg, so where it sits in the flow is free. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture star_row -%}
      <use href="#sh-star-{{ section.id }}" x="0" width="20" height="20"/><use href="#sh-star-{{ section.id }}" x="24" width="20" height="20"/><use href="#sh-star-{{ section.id }}" x="48" width="20" height="20"/><use href="#sh-star-{{ section.id }}" x="72" width="20" height="20"/><use href="#sh-star-{{ section.id }}" x="96" width="20" height="20"/>
    {%- endcapture -%}
    <svg class="sh-pdp__stars-defs" width="0" height="0" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <defs>
        <symbol id="sh-star-{{ section.id }}" viewBox="0 0 22 20" overflow="visible"><path d="M10.525.464a.5.5 0 0 1 .95 0l2.107 6.482a.5.5 0 0 0 .475.346h6.817a.5.5 0 0 1 .294.904l-5.515 4.007a.5.5 0 0 0-.181.559l2.106 6.483a.5.5 0 0 1-.77.559l-5.514-4.007a.5.5 0 0 0-.588 0l-5.514 4.007a.5.5 0 0 1-.77-.56l2.106-6.482a.5.5 0 0 0-.181-.56L.832 8.197a.5.5 0 0 1 .294-.904h6.817a.5.5 0 0 0 .475-.346z"/></symbol>
        <linearGradient id="sh-star-gold-{{ section.id }}" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#ac8940"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#7a5d2e"/></linearGradient>
      </defs>
    </svg>

    {%- if s.show_breadcrumb -%}
      <nav class="sh-pdp__crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a>
        {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'chevron-right', sw: 1.6 %}
        <a href="{{ product.url }}" aria-current="page">{{ product.title }}</a>
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="sh-pdp__grid">

      <div class="sh-pdp__gallery{% if gallery_count > 1 %} sh-pdp__gallery--rail{% endif %}">
        <div class="sh-pdp__stage" data-sh-stage>
          {%- assign gi = 0 -%}
          {%- for media in product.media -%}
            {%- assign gi = gi | plus: 1 -%}
            <figure class="sh-pdp__slide{% if gi == 1 %} is-active{% endif %}"
                    data-media-id="{{ media.id }}">
              <img src="{{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 1100 }}"
                   srcset="{{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w,
                           {{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 740 }} 740w,
                           {{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 1100 }} 1100w,
                           {{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w"
                   sizes="(max-width: 989px) 100vw, 50vw"
                   width="{{ media.preview_image.width }}"
                   height="{{ media.preview_image.height }}"
                   alt="{{ media.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
                   data-large="{{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 2048 }}"
                   {% if gi == 1 %}fetchpriority="high"{% else %}loading="lazy" decoding="async"{% endif %}>
            </figure>
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'gallery_image' and block.settings.image != blank -%}
              {%- assign gi = gi | plus: 1 -%}
              <figure class="sh-pdp__slide{% if gi == 1 %} is-active{% endif %}"
                      data-media-id="b-{{ block.id }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <img src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 1100 }}"
                     srcset="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w,
                             {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 740 }} 740w,
                             {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 1100 }} 1100w,
                             {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w"
                     sizes="(max-width: 989px) 100vw, 50vw"
                     width="{{ block.settings.image.width }}"
                     height="{{ block.settings.image.height }}"
                     alt="{{ block.settings.alt | default: block.settings.image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
                     data-large="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 2048 }}"
                     {% if gi == 1 %}fetchpriority="high"{% else %}loading="lazy" decoding="async"{% endif %}>
              </figure>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- if gallery_count == 0 -%}
            <figure class="sh-pdp__slide is-active">
              {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'sh-pdp__placeholder' }}
            </figure>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if gallery_count > 1 -%}
            <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__nav sh-pdp__nav--prev" data-sh-nav="-1" aria-label="Previous image">
              {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'chevron-left', sw: 1.6 %}
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__nav sh-pdp__nav--next" data-sh-nav="1" aria-label="Next image">
              {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'chevron-right', sw: 1.6 %}
            </button>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.show_zoom and gallery_count > 0 -%}
            <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__zoom" data-sh-zoom aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-label="Zoom image">
              {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'search', sw: 1.6 %}<span>Zoom</span>
            </button>
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="sh-visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-sh-gallery-sr></span>
        </div>

        {%- if gallery_count > 1 -%}
          {%- comment -%} After the stage on purpose — header note 8. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="sh-pdp__thumbs" data-sh-thumbs>
            {%- assign ti = 0 -%}
            {%- for media in product.media -%}
              {%- assign ti = ti | plus: 1 -%}
              <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__thumb" data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
                      aria-label="View image {{ ti }} of {{ gallery_count }}"
                      {% if ti == 1 %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
                <img src="{{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 160 }}" width="80" height="80" alt="" loading="lazy">
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type == 'gallery_image' and block.settings.image != blank -%}
                {%- assign ti = ti | plus: 1 -%}
                <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__thumb" data-media-id="b-{{ block.id }}"
                        aria-label="View image {{ ti }} of {{ gallery_count }}"
                        {% if ti == 1 %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
                  <img src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 160 }}" width="80" height="80" alt="" loading="lazy">
                </button>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="sh-pdp__info">

        <div class="sh-pdp__head">
          <h1 class="sh-pdp__title sh-serif">
            {{ product.title }}
            <span class="sh-pdp__dot{% unless initial.available %} is-out{% endunless %}"
                  data-sh-dot aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="sh-visually-hidden" data-sh-avail-sr>
              {%- if initial.available %}In stock{% else %}Sold out{% endif -%}
            </span>
          </h1>
          {%- if s.show_wishlist -%}
            {% render 'hov-wishlist', product: product %}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if show_rating -%}
          {%- comment -%} Two copies of the same five stars: an outline base and
              a gold layer clipped to --sh-rating, so 4.9 paints nine tenths of
              the fifth star. role="img" sits on the stars alone — a link inside
              role="img" would vanish from the accessibility tree. The count-up
              on the number is shudhi-home.js's site-wide [data-count-to]. {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="sh-pdp__rating" style="--sh-rating:{{ rating_pct }}%">
            <span class="sh-pdp__stars" role="img" aria-label="Rated {{ rating_txt }} out of {{ rating_max | round }}">              <span class="sh-pdp__stars-base" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg class="sh-pdp__stars-svg" viewBox="0 0 116 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">{{ star_row }}</svg>
              </span>
              <span class="sh-pdp__stars-fill" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg class="sh-pdp__stars-svg" viewBox="0 0 116 20" fill="url(#sh-star-gold-{{ section.id }})" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">{{ star_row }}</svg>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="sh-pdp__rating-num sh-serif" aria-hidden="true">{{ rating_txt }}</span>
            {%- if show_reviews -%}
              <a class="sh-pdp__rating-count" href="#sh-reviews"><span data-count-to="{{ rating_count }}">{{ rating_count }}</span> {% if rating_count == 1 %}review{% else %}reviews{% endif %}</a>
            {%- else -%}
              <span class="sh-pdp__rating-count"><span data-count-to="{{ rating_count }}">{{ rating_count }}</span> {% if rating_count == 1 %}review{% else %}reviews{% endif %}</span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%} Short description: the product's custom.short_description
            metafield if set, else the section's copy from templates/product.json. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if product.metafields.custom.short_description.value != blank -%}
          <div class="sh-pdp__blurb">{{ product.metafields.custom.short_description | metafield_tag }}</div>
        {%- elsif s.short_description != blank -%}
          <div class="sh-pdp__blurb"><p>{{ s.short_description }}</p></div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- liquid
          # MRP for the pre-selected pack, resolved exactly the way each pack card
          # below resolves its own: a real compare-at price in admin wins, else the
          # matching "Pack option" block's MRP. Server-rendered so the offer is
          # visible with JS off; sh-product.js then mirrors the checked radio,
          # which carries the same two numbers as data attributes.
          assign lead_mrp = 0
          if initial.compare_at_price > initial.price
            assign lead_mrp = initial.compare_at_price
          endif
          assign lead_pos = 0
          for v in product.variants
            if v.id == initial.id
              assign lead_pos = forloop.index
            endif
          endfor
          assign lead_seen = 0
          for b in section.blocks
            if b.type == 'pack'
              assign lead_seen = lead_seen | plus: 1
              if lead_seen == lead_pos and lead_mrp == 0
                assign lead_mrp = b.settings.mrp | times: 100
              endif
            endif
          endfor
          # An "MRP" at or below the selling price is not an offer — drop it.
          if lead_mrp <= initial.price
            assign lead_mrp = 0
          endif
          assign lead_off = 0
          if lead_mrp > 0
            assign lead_off = lead_mrp | minus: initial.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: lead_mrp | round
          endif
        -%}
        <p class="sh-pdp__cost">
          <span class="sh-pdp__price" data-sh-price>{{ initial.price | money_with_currency }}</span>
          {%- comment -%} .sh-pdp__was / .sh-pdp__off carry no "price" substring, so
              hov-wishlist.js's '[class*="price"]:not([class*="compare"])' scrape
              still lands on .sh-pdp__price above — header note 4. {%- endcomment -%}
          <s class="sh-pdp__was sh-pdp__was--lead{% if lead_mrp == 0 %} is-hidden{% endif %}" data-sh-lead-was>
            <span class="sh-visually-hidden">M.R.P.</span>
            <span data-sh-lead-was-amount>{{ lead_mrp | money }}</span>
          </s>
          <span class="sh-pdp__off{% if lead_off == 0 %} is-hidden{% endif %}" data-sh-lead-off>{{ lead_off }}% OFF</span>
          {%- if s.tax_note != blank -%}
            <span class="sh-pdp__tax">{{ s.tax_note }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>

        {%- liquid
          # "minutes" needs no date to be valid; "date" is dead without one.
          assign cd_on = false
          if s.countdown_enable
            if s.countdown_mode == 'minutes'
              assign cd_on = true
            elsif s.countdown_end_date != blank
              assign cd_on = true
            endif
          endif
        -%}
        {%- if cd_on -%}
          {%- assign cd_time = s.countdown_end_time | default: '23:59' -%}
          <div class="sh-pdp__timer"
               data-sh-timer
               data-sh-timer-mode="{{ s.countdown_mode }}"
               data-sh-timer-minutes="{{ s.countdown_minutes }}"
               {% comment %} Keyed per product, so two PDPs open in one session do
                   not share a window. sh-product.js stamps the deadline against it.
                   Whitespace-trimming this comment would weld the two attributes
                   together. {% endcomment %}
               data-sh-timer-key="sh-pdp-offer-{{ product.id }}"
               data-sh-deadline="{{ s.countdown_end_date }}T{{ cd_time }}"
               hidden>
            <span class="sh-pdp__timer-label">{{ s.countdown_text }}</span>
            <span class="sh-pdp__timer-digits" data-sh-timer-digits aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="sh-visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-sh-timer-sr></span>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {% form 'product', product, id: 'sh-pdp-form', class: 'sh-pdp__form', data-sh-form: '' %}

          <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ initial.id }}" data-sh-id>

          {%- unless product.has_only_default_variant -%}
            <fieldset class="sh-pdp__packs">
              <legend class="sh-visually-hidden">Choose an option</legend>

              {%- liquid
                # The biggest absolute saving gets the "Best value" caption.
                assign max_saving = 0
                for v in product.variants
                  if v.compare_at_price > v.price
                    assign sv = v.compare_at_price | minus: v.price
                    if sv > max_saving
                      assign max_saving = sv
                    endif
                  endif
                endfor
              -%}

              {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
                {%- liquid
                  # "Pack option" blocks pair with variants top to bottom: the 1st
                  # pack block re-titles the 1st variant and so on. A variant with
                  # no block keeps its admin title and the auto captions below, so
                  # adding a variant in admin can never blank a card. forloop is
                  # captured first — the block loop shadows it.
                  assign vidx = forloop.index
                  assign pk_title = ''
                  assign pk_note = ''
                  assign pk_flag = ''
                  assign pk_mrp = 0
                  assign pk_attrs = ''
                  assign pk_seen = 0
                  for b in section.blocks
                    if b.type == 'pack'
                      assign pk_seen = pk_seen | plus: 1
                      if pk_seen == vidx
                        assign pk_title = b.settings.title
                        assign pk_note = b.settings.note
                        assign pk_flag = b.settings.flag
                        assign pk_mrp = b.settings.mrp | times: 100
                        assign pk_attrs = b.shopify_attributes
                      endif
                    endif
                  endfor

                  # MRP. A real compare-at price in admin always wins: it is what
                  # Shopify itself reports and what every other surface (search,
                  # cards, Shop app) already shows. The block's number is the
                  # stand-in until admin carries one, and is ignored unless it is
                  # genuinely above the selling price.
                  assign mrp = 0
                  if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
                    assign mrp = variant.compare_at_price
                  elsif pk_mrp > variant.price
                    assign mrp = pk_mrp
                  endif

                  assign saving = 0
                  assign pct = 0
                  if mrp > 0
                    assign saving = mrp | minus: variant.price
                    assign pct = saving | times: 100.0 | divided_by: mrp | round
                  elsif variant.metafields.custom.discount_percent != blank
                    # No MRP from either source: fall back to the badge the legacy
                    # swatch read (snippets/swatch.liquid:143). Badge only — there is
                    # no struck price or saving to show without a real MRP.
                    assign pct = variant.metafields.custom.discount_percent | plus: 0
                  endif

                  # Price after the checkout coupon. Never rendered below zero, and
                  # never rendered at all when the coupon is switched off.
                  assign final_price = 0
                  if coupon_cents > 0 and variant.price > coupon_cents
                    assign final_price = variant.price | minus: coupon_cents
                  endif

                  assign is_popular = false
                  if forloop.index == s.most_popular_position and variant.available
                    assign is_popular = true
                  endif
                -%}
                <label class="sh-pdp__pack{% if variant.available == false %} is-soldout{% endif %}" {{ pk_attrs }}>
                  {%- comment -%} data-mrp / data-off / data-final hand sh-product.js
                      the numbers Liquid already resolved, so switching packs needs no
                      second copy of this arithmetic in JS. {%- endcomment -%}
                  <input type="radio"
                         class="sh-pdp__pack-input sh-visually-hidden"
                         name="sh-pack-{{ section.id }}"
                         value="{{ variant.id }}"
                         data-variant-id="{{ variant.id }}"
                         data-mrp="{{ mrp }}"
                         data-off="{{ pct }}"
                         data-final="{{ final_price }}"
                         {% if variant.featured_media %}data-media-id="{{ variant.featured_media.id }}"{% endif %}
                         {% if variant.id == initial.id %}checked{% endif %}
                         {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
                  <span class="sh-pdp__pack-card">
                    {%- if pk_flag != blank -%}
                      <span class="sh-pdp__pack-flag">{{ pk_flag | escape }}</span>
                    {%- elsif is_popular -%}
                      <span class="sh-pdp__pack-flag">Most popular</span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    <span class="sh-pdp__pack-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="sh-pdp__pack-main">
                      <span class="sh-pdp__pack-name">
                        {{ pk_title | default: variant.title | escape }}
                        {%- if pct > 0 %}
                          <span class="sh-pdp__pack-off">{{ pct }}% OFF</span>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </span>
                      <span class="sh-pdp__pack-note">
                        {%- if variant.available == false -%}
                          Sold out
                        {%- elsif pk_note != blank -%}
                          {{ pk_note | escape }}
                        {%- elsif saving == 0 -%}
                          Standard price
                        {%- elsif saving == max_saving -%}
                          Best value — biggest saving
                        {%- else -%}
                          You save {{ saving | money }}
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </span>
                    </span>
                    {%- comment -%} A top-down ladder, each rung struck by the one
                        under it: M.R.P. -> pack price -> price with the code. The
                        live number is last and is the only one not struck, so the
                        cut always reads as "down to this". The struck rungs carry
                        a visually-hidden label each — five bare numbers in a row
                        are meaningless read aloud. {%- endcomment -%}
                    <span class="sh-pdp__pack-money">
                      {%- if mrp > 0 -%}
                        <s class="sh-pdp__was">
                          <span class="sh-visually-hidden">M.R.P.</span>
                          {{ mrp | money }}
                        </s>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {%- if final_price > 0 and variant.available -%}
                        <s class="sh-pdp__cut">
                          <span class="sh-visually-hidden">Price before the code</span>
                          {{ variant.price | money }}
                        </s>
                        <span class="sh-pdp__pack-amount sh-pdp__pack-amount--final">{{ final_price | money }}</span>
                        <span class="sh-pdp__pack-with">
                          {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'tag', sw: 1.6 %}with code
                        </span>
                      {%- else -%}
                        <span class="sh-pdp__pack-amount">{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </span>
                  </span>
                </label>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </fieldset>
            <noscript>
              <p class="sh-pdp__noscript">JavaScript is off in your browser — the highlighted option is the one added to the cart.</p>
            </noscript>
          {%- endunless -%}

          {%- comment -%} Both rows follow lead_mrp (resolved above the price row),
              not initial.compare_at_price, so a pack whose MRP comes from its block
              still gets a saving line. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign initial_saving = 0 -%}
          {%- if lead_mrp > initial.price -%}
            {%- assign initial_saving = lead_mrp | minus: initial.price -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          <p class="sh-pdp__saving{% if initial_saving == 0 %} is-hidden{% endif %}"
             data-sh-saving aria-live="polite">
            {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right', sw: 1.6 %}
            <span>You're saving
              <strong data-sh-saving-amount>{{ initial_saving | money }}</strong>
              on this order</span>
          </p>

          {%- if coupon_cents > 0 -%}
            {%- assign initial_final = 0 -%}
            {%- if initial.price > coupon_cents -%}
              {%- assign initial_final = initial.price | minus: coupon_cents -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            <p class="sh-pdp__coupon{% if initial_final == 0 %} is-hidden{% endif %}"
               data-sh-coupon aria-live="polite">
              {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'tag', sw: 1.6 %}
              <span>Extra {{ coupon_cents | money }} off with code
                <b class="sh-pdp__coupon-code">{{ s.coupon_code | escape }}</b>
                — you pay <strong data-sh-coupon-amount>{{ initial_final | money }}</strong> at checkout</span>
            </p>
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="sh-pdp__trust">
            <div class="sh-pdp__trust-item">
              {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'shield' %}
              <span class="sh-pdp__trust-copy">
                {%- if s.trust_line_1 != blank -%}<strong>{{ s.trust_line_1 }}</strong>{%- endif -%}
                {%- if s.trust_line_2 != blank -%}<span>{{ s.trust_line_2 }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="sh-pdp__trust-item">
              {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'lock' %}
              <span class="sh-pdp__trust-copy"><strong>{{ s.trust_secure }}</strong></span>
            </div>
          </div>

          {%- unless settings.enable_catalog_mode -%}
            <div class="sh-pdp__buy" data-sh-buyrow>
              <div class="sh-pdp__qty">
                <button type="button" data-sh-qty="-1" aria-label="Decrease quantity">
                  {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'minus', sw: 1.6 %}
                </button>
                {%- comment -%} type="text", not "number": assets/ajax-cart.js.liquid
                    qtySelectors() replaces EVERY input[type=number] on the page
                    with its own caret widget and removes the original, which
                    would orphan this stepper. clampQty() in sh-product.js keeps
                    the value a whole number >= 1. {%- endcomment -%}
                <input type="text" name="quantity" value="1"
                       inputmode="numeric" pattern="[0-9]*" autocomplete="off"
                       aria-label="Quantity" data-sh-qty-input>
                <button type="button" data-sh-qty="1" aria-label="Increase quantity">
                  {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'plus', sw: 1.6 %}
                </button>
              </div>
              <button type="submit" name="add"
                      class="sh-pdp__atc enj-add-to-cart-btn"
                      data-sh-atc
                      {% unless initial.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
                {%- if initial.available %}Add to cart{% else %}Sold out{% endif -%}
              </button>
            </div>

            <div class="sh-pdp__paybtn">{{ form | payment_button }}</div>
          {%- endunless -%}

        {% endform %}

        {%- if s.dispatch_note != blank -%}
          <p class="sh-pdp__note">
            {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'clock', sw: 1.6 %}
            <span>{{ s.dispatch_note }}</span>
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          FAQ accordion, straight under Buy it now. Native <details>/<summary>:
          `name` makes it one-open-at-a-time in the browser, ::details-content
          in shudhi-product.css animates open AND close (older engines snap —
          still fully usable), and no JS is involved. The "details" block keeps
          the legacy "More Information" rows (snippets/tab-product-details.liquid
          :98-172) so no regulatory copy a merchant entered in admin disappears.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- liquid
          # count the rows that will actually render, so an all-blank block list
          # never leaves an empty bordered box (and a hidden heading) behind
          assign faq_count = 0
          for block in section.blocks
            if block.type == 'details'
              assign faq_count = faq_count | plus: 1
            elsif block.type == 'faq' and block.settings.question != blank and block.settings.answer != blank
              assign faq_count = faq_count | plus: 1
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        {%- if faq_count > 0 -%}
          <div class="sh-pdp__faq">
            {%- comment -%} Keeps the outline h1 -> h2 -> h3 now that the Reviews h2
                only renders with real review data. {%- endcomment -%}
            <h2 class="sh-visually-hidden">Frequently asked questions</h2>
            {%- assign faq_opened = false -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- case block.type -%}
                {%- when 'faq' -%}
                  {%- if block.settings.question != blank and block.settings.answer != blank -%}
                    <details class="sh-pdp__faq-item" name="sh-pdp-faq-{{ section.id }}"
                             {% if s.faq_open_first and faq_opened == false %}open{% endif %}
                             {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                      <summary class="sh-pdp__faq-q">
                        {%- if block.settings.icon != blank and block.settings.icon != 'none' -%}
                          {% render 'sh-icon', name: block.settings.icon, sw: 1.5, class: 'sh-pdp__faq-glyph' %}
                        {%- endif -%}
                        <h3 class="sh-pdp__faq-title">{{ block.settings.question }}</h3>
                        {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'plus', sw: 1.6, class: 'sh-pdp__faq-icon' %}
                      </summary>
                      <div class="sh-pdp__faq-a">
                        <div class="sh-pdp__faq-a-in">{{ block.settings.answer }}</div>
                      </div>
                    </details>
                    {%- assign faq_opened = true -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- when 'details' -%}
                  {%- assign mf = product.metafields.custom -%}
                  <details class="sh-pdp__faq-item" name="sh-pdp-faq-{{ section.id }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <summary class="sh-pdp__faq-q">
                      {%- if block.settings.icon != blank and block.settings.icon != 'none' -%}
                        {% render 'sh-icon', name: block.settings.icon, sw: 1.5, class: 'sh-pdp__faq-glyph' %}
                      {%- endif -%}
                      <h3 class="sh-pdp__faq-title">{{ block.settings.title | default: 'Product details' }}</h3>
                      {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'plus', sw: 1.6, class: 'sh-pdp__faq-icon' %}
                    </summary>
                    <div class="sh-pdp__faq-a">
                      <div class="sh-pdp__faq-a-in">
                        {%- if block.settings.show_description and product.description != blank -%}
                          <div class="sh-pdp__faq-desc">{{ product.description }}</div>
                        {%- endif -%}
                        <dl class="sh-pdp__facts">
                          {%- if mf.brand != blank -%}<dt>Brand</dt><dd>{{ mf.brand }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                          <dt>Country of Origin</dt><dd>India</dd>
                          <dt>Marketed by</dt><dd>Shudhi Herbals</dd>
                          {%- if mf.net_weight != blank -%}<dt>Net Weight</dt><dd>{{ mf.net_weight }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                          {%- if mf.unit_price != blank -%}<dt>Unit Price</dt><dd>{{ mf.unit_price }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                          {%- if mf.pack_type != blank -%}<dt>Pack Type</dt><dd>{{ mf.pack_type }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                          {%- if mf.manufacturer != blank -%}<dt>Manufacturer</dt><dd>{{ mf.manufacturer }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                          {%- if mf.manufacturer_address != blank -%}<dt>Manufacturer Address 1</dt><dd>{{ mf.manufacturer_address }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                          {%- if mf.manufacturer_address1 != blank -%}<dt>Manufacturer Address 2</dt><dd>{{ mf.manufacturer_address1 }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                          {%- if mf.shelf_life != blank -%}<dt>Shelf Life</dt><dd>{{ mf.shelf_life }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                          {%- if mf.product_dimension != blank -%}<dt>Product Dimension</dt><dd>{{ mf.product_dimension }}</dd>{%- endif -%}
                        </dl>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </details>
              {%- endcase -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.show_categories and product.collections.size > 0 -%}
          <p class="sh-pdp__meta">
            <span class="sh-pdp__meta-label">Categories:</span>
            {% for c in product.collections -%}
              <a href="{{ c.url }}">{{ c.title }}</a>{%- unless forloop.last %}, {% endunless -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </p>
        {%- endif -%}

      </div>

      {%- if s.show_perks and perk_count > 0 -%}
        <ul class="sh-pdp__perks" role="list">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'perk' and block.settings.title != blank -%}
              <li class="sh-pdp__perk" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {% render 'sh-icon', name: block.settings.icon, sw: 1.3 %}
                <span class="sh-pdp__perk-copy">
                  <b>{{ block.settings.title }}</b>
                  {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}<small>{{ block.settings.text }}</small>{%- endif -%}
                </span>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if s.show_why and why_count > 0 -%}
        {%- assign why_photo = s.why_bg_strength | default: 18 | divided_by: 100.0 -%}
        <div class="sh-pdp__why" style="--sh-pdp-why-photo:{{ why_photo }}">
          {%- if s.why_bg_image != blank -%}
            <img class="sh-pdp__why-bg" src="{{ s.why_bg_image | image_url: width: 1400 }}" alt=""
                 width="1400" height="{{ 1400 | divided_by: s.why_bg_image.aspect_ratio | round }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          {%- else -%}
            <img class="sh-pdp__why-bg" src="{{ 'Transform your daily Bath.webp' | asset_url }}" alt=""
                 width="2000" height="1100" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          {%- endif -%}
          <div class="sh-pdp__why-in">
            {%- if s.why_heading != blank or s.why_heading_em != blank -%}
              <h2 class="sh-pdp__why-title sh-serif">{{ s.why_heading }}{% if s.why_heading_em != blank %} <em>{{ s.why_heading_em }}</em>{% endif %}</h2>
            {%- endif -%}
            <ul class="sh-pdp__why-grid" role="list">
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                {%- if block.type == 'why' and block.settings.title != blank -%}
                  <li class="sh-pdp__why-item" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <span class="sh-pdp__why-icon">{% render 'sh-icon', name: block.settings.icon, sw: 1.3 %}</span>
                    <h3 class="sh-pdp__why-label">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
                    {%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}<p class="sh-pdp__why-text">{{ block.settings.text | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Key ingredients — a full-grid-width band between the two-column grid and
      the trust ribbon. Three things are worth knowing here:

      a. THE COUNT RUNS FIRST. Same rule as the FAQ above: an all-blank block
         list must leave no heading and no empty bordered row behind, so the
         band is gated on a counted total rather than on section.blocks.size.
      b. THE PHOTO IS CENTRE-CROPPED TO A CIRCLE BY CSS, not by a Liquid crop
         param. asset_img_url has no crop argument, so '480x' only constrains
         width; .sh-pdp__ing-media does the round mask and object-fit: cover.
         That is why the img carries no square dimensions of its own.
      c. THE ASSET BRANCH IS THE ONE IN USE. The ingredient photographs ship in
         the theme's Assets folder, so blocks name a filename rather than a
         merchant upload. The image_picker still wins when one is chosen, which
         keeps the band editable without re-uploading anything to Files.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign ing_count = 0
      for block in section.blocks
        if block.type == 'ingredient' and block.settings.title != blank
          assign ing_count = ing_count | plus: 1
        endif
      endfor
    -%}
    {%- if s.show_ingredients and ing_count > 0 -%}
      <div class="sh-pdp__ing">
        {%- if s.ingredients_heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="sh-pdp__ing-title sh-serif">{{ s.ingredients_heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        <ul class="sh-pdp__ing-grid" role="list">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'ingredient' and block.settings.title != blank -%}
              {%- assign b = block.settings -%}
              <li class="sh-pdp__ing-card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                {%- if b.image != blank or b.asset != blank -%}
                  <span class="sh-pdp__ing-media">
                    {%- if b.image != blank -%}
                      <img src="{{ b.image | image_url: width: 480 }}"
                           alt="{{ b.image.alt | default: b.title | escape }}"
                           width="480" height="{{ 480 | divided_by: b.image.aspect_ratio | round }}"
                           loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                    {%- else -%}
                      <img src="{{ b.asset | asset_img_url: '480x' }}"
                           alt="{{ b.title | escape }}"
                           width="480" height="320" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}
                <h3 class="sh-pdp__ing-name">{{ b.title }}</h3>
                {%- if b.text != blank -%}<p class="sh-pdp__ing-text">{{ b.text | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Benefits — a blush card of icon tiles, between the ingredient band and
      the trust ribbon. Three things worth knowing:

      a. THE COUNT RUNS FIRST. Same rule as the FAQ and the ingredient band
         above: an all-blank block list must leave no heading and no empty
         blush card behind, so the band is gated on a counted total rather
         than on section.blocks.size.
      b. THE COLUMN COUNT IS FIXED AT SIX, not auto-fit, and the block limit
         is 6 to match. Six is the designed row; auto-fit would quietly
         reflow a seventh tile into a ragged second row instead of making the
         over-count visible in the editor.
      c. THE GLYPHS ARE DECORATIVE. Every tile's meaning is carried by its
         visible label, and sh-icon already emits aria-hidden, so there is no
         second accessible name to write here. That is also why the tile has
         no sub-copy: this band is a spec strip, not a second pitch.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign ben_count = 0
      for block in section.blocks
        if block.type == 'benefit' and block.settings.title != blank
          assign ben_count = ben_count | plus: 1
        endif
      endfor
    -%}
    {%- if s.show_benefits and ben_count > 0 -%}
      <div class="sh-pdp__ben">
        {%- if s.benefits_heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="sh-pdp__ben-title sh-serif">{{ s.benefits_heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        <ul class="sh-pdp__ben-grid" role="list">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == 'benefit' and block.settings.title != blank -%}
              <li class="sh-pdp__ben-card" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                <span class="sh-pdp__ben-icon">{% render 'sh-icon', name: block.settings.icon, sw: 1.3 %}</span>
                <h3 class="sh-pdp__ben-label">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
              </li>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Trust ribbon — the homepage marquee (sections/sh-trust-marquee.liquid),
      icons only, sitting under the buy column's FAQ and above the proof band.
      It reuses .sh-tmarquee wholesale — same medallions, same glyphs, same
      loop — and shudhi-product.css only undoes the band background and the
      section-sized padding a full-width section needs and a strip does not.

      Three things carry over from that section verbatim:

      a. THE DEFS ARE RENDERED ONCE, ABOVE BOTH PASSES. The track duplicates
         every item so translateX(-50%) can loop seamlessly, so each glyph
         exists twice. Rendering the gradients inside the icon would emit
         sixteen copies of the same ids — duplicate DEFINITIONS, which are
         invalid and silently collapse to the first. The full reasoning is in
         snippets/sh-trust-icon.liquid:20-31.
      b. THE SECOND PASS CARRIES aria-hidden. shudhi-home.css:5116 hides
         `.sh-tmarquee__group[aria-hidden="true"]` under reduced motion, so the
         wrapped static layout shows the set once rather than twice.
      c. THE STRIP IS DECORATIVE, and that is why aria-hidden sits on the root
         too. It carries no labels by design, so there is no claim here for a
         screen reader to read; announcing eight certifications that no sighted
         visitor can read on this page would be worse than saying nothing.

      The icon list mirrors the homepage block order in templates/index.json.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign rib_gid = 'sh-pdp-tm-' | append: section.id -%}
    {%- assign rib_icons = 'lab,iso,batch,sls,paraben,toxin,cruelty,natural' | split: ',' -%}
    <div class="sh-tmarquee sh-tmarquee--icons sh-tmarquee--ruled sh-tmarquee--hoverpause"
         style="--sh-tm-icon:68px;--sh-tm-speed:31s;" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- comment -%} See (a). Must precede any icon that references it. {%- endcomment -%}
      {% render 'sh-trust-icon', mode: 'defs', gid: rib_gid %}
      <div class="sh-tmarquee__viewport">
        <div class="sh-tmarquee__track">
          {%- for pass in (1..2) -%}
            <ul class="sh-tmarquee__group"{% if forloop.index == 2 %} aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}>
              {%- for ic in rib_icons -%}
                <li class="sh-tmarquee__item">
                  <span class="sh-tmarquee__medallion">
                    {% render 'sh-trust-icon', mode: 'icon', name: ic, gid: rib_gid %}
                  </span>
                </li>
              {%- endfor -%}
            </ul>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if s.show_proof -%}
      {%- comment -%} The shipping line follows Theme settings > Cart Drawer, so it
          can never disagree with the drawer's own free-shipping bar. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign fs = settings.free_shipping_threshold | default: 500 -%}
      <div class="sh-pdp__proof{% if s.proof_quote == blank %} sh-pdp__proof--two{% endif %}">
        <div class="sh-pdp__proof-love">
          {%- if s.proof_heading != blank -%}<p class="sh-pdp__proof-title sh-serif">{{ s.proof_heading }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if avatar_count > 0 or s.proof_more != blank -%}
            <div class="sh-pdp__proof-avatars" aria-hidden="true">
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                {%- if block.type == 'avatar' -%}
                  <span class="sh-pdp__avatar" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
                      <img src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 96 }}" width="40" height="40" alt="" loading="lazy">
                    {%- elsif block.settings.name != blank -%}
                      {{- block.settings.name | strip | slice: 0 | upcase -}}
                    {%- else -%}
                      {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'user', sw: 1.5 %}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- if s.proof_more != blank -%}<span class="sh-pdp__avatar sh-pdp__avatar--more">{{ s.proof_more }}</span>{%- endif -%}
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>

        {%- if s.proof_quote != blank -%}
          <figure class="sh-pdp__proof-quote">
            <span class="sh-pdp__stars" role="img" aria-label="Rated {{ s.proof_stars }} out of 5" style="--sh-rating:{{ s.proof_stars | times: 20 }}%">
              <span class="sh-pdp__stars-base" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="sh-pdp__stars-svg" viewBox="0 0 116 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">{{ star_row }}</svg></span>
              <span class="sh-pdp__stars-fill" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="sh-pdp__stars-svg" viewBox="0 0 116 20" fill="url(#sh-star-gold-{{ section.id }})" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">{{ star_row }}</svg></span>
            </span>
            <blockquote><p>“{{ s.proof_quote | escape }}”</p></blockquote>
            {%- if s.proof_author != blank -%}<figcaption>— {{ s.proof_author | escape }}</figcaption>{%- endif -%}
          </figure>
        {%- endif -%}

        <ul class="sh-pdp__proof-tiles" role="list">
          {%- if s.tile_1_title != blank -%}
            <li class="sh-pdp__proof-tile">
              {% render 'sh-icon', name: s.tile_1_icon %}
              <span class="sh-pdp__proof-tile-copy">
                <b>{{ s.tile_1_title }}</b>
                <small>{% if s.tile_1_text != blank %}{{ s.tile_1_text }}{% else %}On orders above {{ fs | times: 100 | money_without_trailing_zeros }}{% endif %}</small>
              </span>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if s.tile_2_title != blank -%}
            <li class="sh-pdp__proof-tile">
              {% render 'sh-icon', name: s.tile_2_icon %}
              <span class="sh-pdp__proof-tile-copy">
                <b>{{ s.tile_2_title }}</b>
                {%- if s.tile_2_text != blank -%}<small>{{ s.tile_2_text }}</small>{%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        </ul>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if show_reviews -%}
      <div class="sh-pdp__reviews" id="sh-reviews">
        <h2 class="sh-pdp__reviews-title sh-serif">Reviews</h2>
        {%- comment -%} Same Judge.me embed the legacy tabs used
            (snippets/tab-product-details.liquid:91-93). {%- endcomment -%}
        <div id="judgeme_product_reviews" class="jdgm-widget jdgm-review-widget" data-id="{{ product.id }}">
          {{ product.metafields.judgeme.widget }}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>

  {%- if s.sticky_bar -%}
    {%- comment -%} Rendered LAST inside the section on purpose: hov-wishlist.js's
        price scrape takes the first '[class*="price"]' in DOM order, and this bar
        repeats the price. See note 4 in the header. Hidden until sh-product.js
        shows it on mobile after the buy row scrolls away. {%- endcomment -%}
    <aside class="sh-pdp__sticky" data-sh-sticky hidden aria-hidden="true">
      {%- if product.featured_image -%}
        <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 96 }}"
             width="48" height="48" alt="" loading="lazy">
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="sh-pdp__sticky-txt">
        <span class="sh-pdp__sticky-title" data-sh-sticky-title>
          {%- if product.has_only_default_variant %}{{ product.title }}{% else %}{{ initial.title }}{% endif -%}
        </span>
        <span class="sh-pdp__sticky-amt" data-sh-sticky-amt>{{ initial.price | money }}</span>
      </span>
      <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__sticky-atc" data-sh-sticky-atc
              {% unless initial.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
        {%- if initial.available %}Add to cart{% else %}Sold out{% endif -%}
      </button>
    </aside>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if gallery_count > 0 -%}
    {%- comment -%} Zoom viewer. No src on the image until it opens, so nothing
        loads for visitors who never zoom. Header note 8. {%- endcomment -%}
    <dialog class="sh-pdp__lightbox" data-sh-lightbox aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }} — image viewer">
      <div class="sh-pdp__lb-bar">
        <span class="sh-pdp__lb-count" data-sh-lb-count aria-live="polite"></span>
        <span class="sh-pdp__lb-actions">
          <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__lb-btn" data-sh-lb-zoom aria-label="Magnify" aria-pressed="false">{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'search', sw: 1.6 %}</button>
          <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__lb-btn" data-sh-lb-close aria-label="Close">{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'close', sw: 1.6 %}</button>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="sh-pdp__lb-stage" data-sh-lb-stage>
        <img class="sh-pdp__lb-img" data-sh-lb-img alt="" decoding="async">
      </div>
      {%- if gallery_count > 1 -%}
        <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__lb-btn sh-pdp__lb-nav sh-pdp__lb-nav--prev" data-sh-lb-nav="-1" aria-label="Previous image">{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'chevron-left', sw: 1.6 %}</button>
        <button type="button" class="sh-pdp__lb-btn sh-pdp__lb-nav sh-pdp__lb-nav--next" data-sh-lb-nav="1" aria-label="Next image">{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'chevron-right', sw: 1.6 %}</button>
      {%- endif -%}
    </dialog>
  {%- endif -%}

  <script type="application/json" data-sh-variants>{{ product.variants | json }}</script>
</section>

<script src="{{ 'sh-product.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- comment -%} Stops the trust ribbon compositing while it is off screen, and
    does nothing else. It can only ever ADD .is-paused, so a 404 or an exception
    leaves the ribbon running rather than parked — the polarity that file's
    header argues for at length. {%- endcomment -%}
<script src="{{ 'sh-trust-marquee.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SH · Product",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Layout" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_breadcrumb", "label": "Show breadcrumb", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_wishlist", "label": "Show wishlist heart", "default": true },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg", "label": "Background", "default": "#fdfbf7",
      "info": "Keep it light — the pack cards, trust panel and gold button are tuned for a light surface." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pad_top", "label": "Top padding", "min": 0, "max": 80, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 24 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pad_bottom", "label": "Bottom padding", "min": 0, "max": 80, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 48 },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Rating & short description" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "rating_value", "label": "Star rating (manual fallback)", "min": 0, "max": 5, "step": 0.1, "default": 4.9,
      "info": "Used only until a reviews app fills Shopify's standard reviews.rating metafield on the product — real data then takes over automatically. Manual numbers never reach search engines." },
    { "type": "number", "id": "rating_count", "label": "Review count (manual fallback)", "default": 52,
      "info": "0 hides the whole star row." },
    { "type": "inline_richtext", "id": "short_description", "label": "Short description",
      "default": "A <b>handmade Ayurvedic cleansing bar</b>, crafted in small batches with <b>herbs and pure essential oils</b>. Free from SLS, SLES, parabens and harsh chemicals, it turns an everyday wash into a calm, grounding ritual to <b>purify, protect and renew</b>. Cruelty free, lab tested, 100 g.",
      "info": "Two or three lines under the rating; bold the phrases that matter. A product's custom.short_description metafield overrides this." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Pack options" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "most_popular_position", "label": "\"Most popular\" option", "min": 1, "max": 6, "step": 1, "default": 2,
      "info": "Which option gets the badge and is pre-selected, counted top to bottom. Ignored when that option is sold out, when the product has a single variant, or when the visitor arrives on a link to a specific option." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Offer countdown" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "countdown_enable", "label": "Enable countdown", "default": false },
    { "type": "text", "id": "countdown_text", "label": "Countdown text", "default": "Hurry! Offer expires in" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "countdown_mode", "label": "Countdown type", "default": "minutes",
      "options": [
        { "value": "minutes", "label": "Limited period — minutes from arrival" },
        { "value": "date", "label": "Fixed end date" }
      ],
      "info": "\"Minutes\" runs a short window per shopper, shown as MM:SS. \"Fixed end date\" counts to one moment for everybody and uses the two date fields below." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "countdown_minutes", "label": "Minutes on the clock", "min": 5, "max": 60, "step": 5, "unit": "min", "default": 10,
      "info": "\"Minutes\" type only. The window is stamped once per browsing session, so moving between pages does not hand the shopper a fresh clock, and it does not restart after it runs out." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "countdown_end_date", "label": "Offer end date",
      "info": "\"Fixed end date\" type only. YYYY-MM-DD, e.g. 2026-09-15. Leave empty to hide the countdown." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "countdown_end_time", "label": "Offer end time", "default": "23:59",
      "info": "24-hour HH:MM, in each shopper's local time. The countdown hides itself once this moment passes — it never restarts per visit." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Checkout coupon" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "coupon_enable", "label": "Show the coupon line", "default": true,
      "info": "Advertises a discount code on each pack and under the pack list. The theme cannot apply it — create the code in Shopify admin > Discounts first, or shoppers will hit a dead code at checkout." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "coupon_code", "label": "Discount code", "default": "SHUDHI50",
      "info": "Must match the code in admin exactly, including case." },
    { "type": "number", "id": "coupon_value", "label": "Amount off", "default": 50,
      "info": "In rupees, not paise. A flat amount off the pack price — set the same value on the admin discount." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Trust panel" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "trust_line_1", "label": "Left title", "default": "No hidden fees" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "trust_line_2", "label": "Left text", "default": "Discounts & gifts will be applied at checkout" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "trust_secure", "label": "Right title", "default": "100% Secure Checkout" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tax_note", "label": "Note beside the price", "default": "(Inc of all taxes.)" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Mobile sticky bar" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "sticky_bar", "label": "Show sticky add-to-cart bar", "default": true,
      "info": "Phones and tablets only. Appears once the buy buttons scroll out of view." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Gallery" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_zoom", "label": "Show the Zoom button", "default": true,
      "info": "Opens a full-screen viewer. Add \"Gallery image\" blocks for photos that are not on the product itself." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Benefit strip" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_perks", "label": "Show the strip under the gallery", "default": true,
      "info": "Built from the \"Benefit\" blocks. Hidden when there are none." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Why you'll love it" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_why", "label": "Show the panel", "default": true,
      "info": "Built from the \"Why you'll love it\" blocks. Hidden when there are none." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "why_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Why You’ll Love It" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "why_heading_em", "label": "Heading — gold words" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "why_bg_image", "label": "Background photo",
      "info": "Faint, behind the text. Without one the theme's forest photo is used." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "why_bg_strength", "label": "Photo strength", "min": 0, "max": 60, "step": 2, "unit": "%", "default": 18 },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Key ingredients" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_ingredients", "label": "Show the band", "default": true,
      "info": "Built from the \"Key ingredient\" blocks. Hidden when there are none." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "ingredients_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Key Ingredients" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Benefits band" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_benefits", "label": "Show the band", "default": true,
      "info": "Built from the \"Benefits tile\" blocks. Hidden when there are none." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "benefits_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Benefits" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Social proof bar" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_proof", "label": "Show the bar", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "proof_heading", "label": "Headline", "default": "Loved by 10,000+ customers",
      "info": "Shown to every visitor — keep it to a number you can stand behind." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "proof_more", "label": "Avatar chip", "default": "+10K" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "proof_stars", "label": "Stars", "min": 1, "max": 5, "step": 1, "default": 5 },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "proof_quote", "label": "Quote",
      "info": "A real customer review, quoted with permission. Leave empty to hide the middle column." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "proof_author", "label": "Quote author", "info": "First name and initial, e.g. \"Priya S.\"" },
    { "type": "select", "id": "tile_1_icon", "label": "Tile 1 icon", "default": "truck",
      "options": [ { "value": "truck", "label": "Truck" }, { "value": "badge", "label": "Badge" }, { "value": "shield", "label": "Shield" }, { "value": "clock", "label": "Clock" }, { "value": "heart-check", "label": "Heart with check" }, { "value": "lock", "label": "Lock" }, { "value": "leaf", "label": "Leaf" } ] },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tile_1_title", "label": "Tile 1 title", "default": "Free shipping" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tile_1_text", "label": "Tile 1 text",
      "info": "Leave empty to show \"On orders above <threshold>\", which follows Theme settings > Cart Drawer > Free shipping threshold." },
    { "type": "select", "id": "tile_2_icon", "label": "Tile 2 icon", "default": "badge",
      "options": [ { "value": "truck", "label": "Truck" }, { "value": "badge", "label": "Badge" }, { "value": "shield", "label": "Shield" }, { "value": "clock", "label": "Clock" }, { "value": "heart-check", "label": "Heart with check" }, { "value": "lock", "label": "Lock" }, { "value": "leaf", "label": "Leaf" } ] },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tile_2_title", "label": "Tile 2 title", "default": "Safe delivery" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "tile_2_text", "label": "Tile 2 text", "default": "Damaged or wrong item? We replace it" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Below the buy box" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "dispatch_note", "label": "Note above the FAQ",
      "info": "Gold pill under Buy it now, e.g. \"Same-day dispatch for orders placed before 1 PM (Mon–Sat)\". Leave empty to hide." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "faq_open_first", "label": "Open the first FAQ by default", "default": false },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_categories", "label": "Show categories", "default": true },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_reviews", "label": "Show reviews", "default": true,
      "info": "Renders only once a reviews app has written data for this product." }
  ],
    "max_blocks": 40,
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "pack", "name": "Pack option", "limit": 6, "settings": [
      { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Pack options pair with the product's variants top to bottom — the first of these re-dresses the first variant. A variant with no block keeps its admin title. The price charged is always the variant's own price in Shopify admin; nothing here changes it." },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Name", "default": "Buy 1 — Standard Pack",
        "info": "Replaces the variant title on the card, e.g. \"Buy 3 — Ritual Pack\". Leave empty to keep the admin title." },
      { "type": "text", "id": "note", "label": "Sub-line", "default": "Perfect to experience the ritual" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "flag", "label": "Badge",
        "info": "The pill above the card, e.g. \"⭐ Most Popular\". Leave empty and the card falls back to the \"Most popular\" position set above." },
      { "type": "number", "id": "mrp", "label": "M.R.P.",
        "info": "In rupees, not paise — the struck-through price the discount is calculated from. IGNORED once this variant has a real compare-at price in Shopify admin, which is the better place for it, and ignored if it is not above the selling price." }
    ] },
    { "type": "faq", "name": "FAQ", "settings": [
      { "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon before the question", "default": "leaf",
        "options": [ { "value": "none", "label": "None" }, { "value": "bubbles", "label": "Lather" }, { "value": "leaf", "label": "Leaf" }, { "value": "face-sparkle", "label": "Glowing skin" }, { "value": "clock", "label": "Clock" }, { "value": "truck", "label": "Truck" }, { "value": "file", "label": "Document" }, { "value": "drop", "label": "Drop" }, { "value": "sparkle", "label": "Sparkle" }, { "value": "shield", "label": "Shield" }, { "value": "mail", "label": "Mail" }, { "value": "badge", "label": "Badge" } ] },
      { "type": "text", "id": "question", "label": "Question", "default": "How do I use the bar?" },
      { "type": "richtext", "id": "answer", "label": "Answer",
        "default": "<p>Work the bar into a light lather with water, massage gently over damp skin, then rinse.</p>" }
    ] },
    { "type": "details", "name": "Product details", "limit": 1, "settings": [
      { "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon before the title", "default": "file",
        "options": [ { "value": "none", "label": "None" }, { "value": "file", "label": "Document" }, { "value": "badge", "label": "Badge" }, { "value": "leaf", "label": "Leaf" }, { "value": "shield", "label": "Shield" }, { "value": "mail", "label": "Mail" } ] },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Row title", "default": "Product details" },
      { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_description", "label": "Include the product description", "default": false,
        "info": "Off by default: this product's admin description only repeats the title." }
    ] },
    { "type": "gallery_image", "name": "Gallery image", "limit": 4, "settings": [
      { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image",
        "info": "Shown after the product's own photos, in block order. Square images match the main photo; other shapes are cropped square here and shown whole in Zoom." },
      { "type": "text", "id": "alt", "label": "Alt text", "info": "Falls back to the image's own alt text, then the product title." }
    ] },
    { "type": "perk", "name": "Benefit", "limit": 4, "settings": [
      { "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon", "default": "leaf-line",
        "options": [ { "value": "lotus", "label": "Lotus" }, { "value": "hand-line", "label": "Hand" }, { "value": "rabbit-line", "label": "Rabbit" }, { "value": "flask-line", "label": "Flask" }, { "value": "leaf-line", "label": "Leaf" }, { "value": "heart-line", "label": "Heart" }, { "value": "mortar", "label": "Mortar & pestle" }, { "value": "wheat", "label": "Wheat" }, { "value": "badge", "label": "Badge" }, { "value": "shield", "label": "Shield" }, { "value": "sparkle", "label": "Sparkle" }, { "value": "drop", "label": "Drop" }, { "value": "recycle", "label": "Recycle" }, { "value": "sun", "label": "Sun" } ] },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "Ayurvedic" },
      { "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Sub-label", "default": "Time-honoured herbs" }
    ] },
    { "type": "why", "name": "Why you'll love it — item", "limit": 4, "settings": [
      { "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon", "default": "sparkle",
        "options": [ { "value": "sparkle", "label": "Sparkle" }, { "value": "shield", "label": "Shield" }, { "value": "leaf-line", "label": "Leaf" }, { "value": "meditate", "label": "Meditate" }, { "value": "lotus", "label": "Lotus" }, { "value": "drop", "label": "Drop" }, { "value": "sun", "label": "Sun" }, { "value": "heart-check", "label": "Heart with check" }, { "value": "hands-heart", "label": "Hands & heart" }, { "value": "face-sparkle", "label": "Glowing skin" }, { "value": "bubbles", "label": "Lather" }, { "value": "plant", "label": "Plant" } ] },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "default": "Purifies Energy" },
      { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Text", "info": "Two short lines read best." }
    ] },
    { "type": "ingredient", "name": "Key ingredient", "limit": 4, "settings": [
      { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photo",
        "info": "Shown in a circle. Anything not square is centre-cropped, so keep the subject central." },
      { "type": "text", "id": "asset", "label": "Fallback image file (in Assets)",
        "info": "Filename of an image already in the theme's Assets folder — the ingredient photographs ship there. Used only when no photo is picked above." },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Name", "default": "Sage" },
      { "type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Description", "info": "Two short lines read best." }
    ] },
    { "type": "benefit", "name": "Benefits tile", "limit": 6, "settings": [
      { "type": "paragraph", "content": "The six-tile blush band under Key ingredients. Distinct from \"Benefit\", which is the icon strip under the gallery." },
      { "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "Icon", "default": "aura",
        "options": [ { "value": "aura", "label": "Aura" }, { "value": "no-negativity", "label": "No negativity" }, { "value": "calm-mind", "label": "Calm mind" }, { "value": "hand", "label": "Hand" }, { "value": "mortar", "label": "Mortar & pestle" }, { "value": "oil-drop", "label": "Oil drop" }, { "value": "lotus", "label": "Lotus" }, { "value": "leaf-line", "label": "Leaf" }, { "value": "hand-line", "label": "Hands" }, { "value": "heart-line", "label": "Heart" }, { "value": "sparkle", "label": "Sparkle" }, { "value": "shield", "label": "Shield" }, { "value": "flask-line", "label": "Flask" }, { "value": "drop", "label": "Drop" } ] },
      { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Label", "default": "Aura Cleansing",
        "info": "One or two words. Shown in small caps — anything longer wraps to a second line." }
    ] },
    { "type": "avatar", "name": "Customer avatar", "limit": 5, "settings": [
      { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photo", "info": "Square, at least 96×96. Without a photo a neutral circle with the initial is shown." },
      { "type": "text", "id": "name", "label": "Name (for the initial)", "info": "Optional. Only the first letter is shown." }
    ] }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
